flowchart TB
    accTitle: Restore a complete local snapshot
    accDescr: Snapshot restore requires current vault authorization and explicit replacement confirmation. The current Master Password authorizes replacement; the snapshot Master Password authenticates the selected historical pair. Staged verification checks the key, Authenticator and payload, with deadline rechecks before commit. Successful replacement ends login; historical credentials and security settings become active again.
    select["Backup Center: select snapshot\nConfirm replacement of current vault"] --> current{"Current vault access and\ncurrent Master Password valid?"}
    current -->|No / expired / cancel| reject["Reject restore\nPreserve live pair"]:::danger
    current -->|Yes| files["Read selected .config + .storage\nValidate ID, bounded files and complete pair"]
    files --> verify["Authenticate snapshot Master slot\nUse snapshot password if different"]
    verify --> contents{"Snapshot key, Authenticator\nand decrypted payload valid?"}
    contents -->|No| reject
    contents -->|Yes| stage[["Stage verified historical pair\nRecheck current authorization"]]
    stage --> token["Remove compatibility unlock token\nSnapshot current pair before replacement"]
    token --> commit{"Paired replacement succeeds?"}
    commit -->|Failure| rollback["Report failure\nAttempt restoration of live pair"]:::danger
    commit -->|Success| logout["Clear login, DEK and decrypted data"]
    logout --> signin["Sign in with restored Master Password\nand restored Authenticator"]:::good
    classDef danger fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b
    classDef good fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d
